= Fear

After the collapse of the Austrian bank Creditanstalt [? if banking_crisis_seen : and our German Danat Bank?], and the subsequent trapping of investor currency to avoid further fallout. Great Britain faced an immense outpour of gold, leaving their reserves dangerously low. In addition to the collapsing global price level, and increasing mass unemployment. Their government has passed a bill suspending the gold standard!

Many are quick to criticize this action, stating fears of inflation and loss of public trust. But time will tell if this proves to be successful

